<$fill $name="body">

!! Link the new tiddler to the drop target

The usual setup: the new tiddler's `parent` field names the tiddler you dropped on. Create this tiddler in your wiki:

```
title: $:/config/rimir/drop-attach/actions/link-parent
tags: $:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/action

<$action-setfield $tiddler=<<new>> parent=<<target>>/>
```

Any field works the same way, e.g. `attachment-of=<<target>>`.

!! Add more fields

```
title: $:/config/rimir/drop-attach/actions/fields
tags: $:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/action

<$action-setfield $tiddler=<<new>> caption=<<filename>> tags="attachment"/>
```

!! List the target in a field of the target

```
title: $:/config/rimir/drop-attach/actions/list-on-target
tags: $:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/action

<$action-listops $tiddler=<<target>> $field="attachments" $subfilter="[<new>]"/>
```

!! Show attachments at a fixed place in the target

The shipped action appends `<<derived-view """<title>""">>` at the end of the tiddler you drop on. To show them somewhere else, switch it off (`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/append` = `no`), link with `parent` (example above) and list them where you like, e.g. full views of all attached files:

```
<$list filter="[parent<currentTiddler>is[binary]]">
<$transclude $variable="derived-view" tiddler=<<currentTiddler>> mode="full"/>
</$list>
```

!! Keep attachments in one folder per day

`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/title-filter`:

```
[<now YYYY-0MM-0DD>addprefix[attachments/]addsuffix[/]addsuffix<filename>]
```

